          "id": "worksheet",
          "title": "Governance Analysis Worksheet",
          "eyebrow": "Analyze a task",
          "description": "Choose a real task and specify its requirements, decision authority, control points, evidence, and outstanding responsibilities.",
          "group": "practice",
          "locale": "en",
          "minutes": 2,
          "source": "content/en/worksheet.md",
          "html": "<h1>Governance Analysis Worksheet</h1>\n<p><a href=\"#/\">Back to home</a></p>\n<p>Choose a specific task and identify what the relevant responsibility must cover. Clear participants, objects, conditions, and evidence matter more than a list of mechanism names. Motivating cases belong directly in the explanation of why a responsibility is needed on its page. This worksheet supports analysis rather than providing a separate case study.</p>\n<h2 id=\"worksheet-s1\">Task and responsibility</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Question</th>\n<th>What to record</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>What is the task?</td>\n<td>Goal, deliverables, mandatory conditions, and deadline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Which responsibility is being analyzed?</td>\n<td>The governance function in focus; do not expand every issue at once</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Why is it needed?</td>\n<td>The concrete failure path without that function, its effects, and why other responsibilities do not cover it</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Where do the requirements come from?</td>\n<td>The mandate, organizational rules, information-use conditions, and who may revise them</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>What is permitted?</td>\n<td>Participants, information, tools, operational scope, resource budget, and authorization validity period</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who is responsible?</td>\n<td>Who judges, executes, and reviews, and which functions existing programs already perform</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"worksheet-s2\">Execution and evidence</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Question</th>\n<th>What to record</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>What is visible?</td>\n<td>Proposals, calls, returns, external state, progress, and unobservable parts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>At which step does failure occur?</td>\n<td>A concrete error, omission, stall, or unknown state in an execution</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>How should the system respond?</td>\n<td>Response conditions, time limits, executable actions, and takeover paths</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>What authority is needed for the response?</td>\n<td>Current permissions for retries, corrections, changes, pauses, or handoffs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>What happens while waiting?</td>\n<td>What may continue, what must pause, and who remains responsible</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>How is the outcome confirmed?</td>\n<td>Checks of actual state, affected scope, necessary conditions, and unknown parts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>What is retained?</td>\n<td>Links among requirements, approvals, actions, effects, anomalies, verification, and responsibility</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>How are records protected?</td>\n<td>Conditions for access, retention, deletion, and minimization of sensitive information</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"worksheet-s3\">Checks before writing a responsibility page</h2>\n<p>Can one case explain the responsibility? If it requires a growing collection of exceptions, roles, and systems to work, first choose a clearer failure path.</p>\n<p>If the draft says only “monitoring agent,” “human confirmation,” “logging,” or “automatic recovery,” explain what it actually observes, decides, changes, or establishes. When using a success message, state the scope of the conclusion it supports. When claiming a responsibility is necessary, also identify which existing arrangements already perform the required functions.</p>",
